  "historical_output_text": " One chilly winter, during middle years I found myself with less experience at my desk in an old-fashioned school office in our city’s primary education. This place of paper-pusher duties had me at once bewildred but I had an easy smile on face that was to greet visitors and their kids and direct those who wandered.\n\nThe office phone would go off with an occasional ringing to break silence that filled the day, with calls about lost books by young learners in search. There once rang in such phone that morning as one student named Alex asked where a book about cats and the moon, with pretty paintings and fun raps in text had ended at",
